eigen-expokit
=============

No third-party source tree is bundled here.  But EXPOKIT is still involved
in two ways:


1. EXPOKIT is fetched on demand -- NON-COMMERCIAL ONLY
------------------------------------------------------

Configuring with -DEXPOKIT_BUILD_FORTRAN=ON downloads the original EXPOKIT
distribution (Fortran 77 and MATLAB) by Roger B. Sidje, Department of
Mathematics, University of Queensland, from
https://www.maths.uq.edu.au/expokit/expokit.tar.gz.

EXPOKIT's notice, quoted verbatim from the tree's `copyright` file, grants
use for NON-COMMERCIAL PURPOSES ONLY.  That restriction means EXPOKIT is
not open source under either the OSI or the FSF definition, and it is not
compatible with MPL-2.0.  Enabling that option therefore pulls restricted
material into the build tree:

